(2470032, 337759, 59155, '<td valign="top">I know this isnt really "success," but it was my first challenge, I had just registered for DPC, and I wanted soooo badly to enter something so I tried to find a picture taken during the challenge time period that looked "success-ey."  Oh well.  Thanks for the comments everyone!  To answer a couple questions  1) I did notice that the picture looks tilted, but thats actually just a weird effect of taking beach pictures from a non-straight-on angle, you can either get the land straight or the water straight, but not both, and in this case I thought having the silhouette correct was more important   2) Im not sure what the "artifact" is, but if youre referring to the land behind the person, it was part of a long penninsula off in the distance.  Thanks again everyone!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-05-31 00:15:22.</i></td>', 'I know this isnt really "success," but it was my first challenge, I had just registered for DPC, and I wanted soooo badly to enter something so I tried to find a picture taken during the challenge time period that looked "success-ey."  Oh well.  Thanks for the comments everyone!  To answer a couple questions  1) I did notice that the picture looks tilted, but thats actually just a weird effect of taking beach pictures from a non-straight-on angle, you can either get the land straight or the water straight, but not both, and in this case I thought having the silhouette correct was more important   2) Im not sure what the "artifact" is, but if youre referring to the land behind the person, it was part of a long penninsula off in the distance.  Thanks again everyone!', '2006-05-31 01:12:32.000000', '2006-05-31 01:15:22.000000', 0),
