(2472326, 338061, 40718, '<td valign="top">I''ll speak to the technical first.  Focus is excellent.  The image is nice and sharp.  There are lighting issues.  The top is too white while the bottom has shadow with color casts.  The composition is static and centered.  That isn''t completely bad because a stock photo of a medal would probably naturally be centered.<br/> <br/>A big limiting factor is the subject holds a lot more interest for you than the casual viewer.  The title, I think, saves it, but not everybody reads the title.  It''s cute to thing how such a cheap trinket would mean so much to a child, but that is only conveyed with the title, not the picture.</td>', 'I''ll speak to the technical first.  Focus is excellent.  The image is nice and sharp.  There are lighting issues.  The top is too white while the bottom has shadow with color casts.  The composition is static and centered.  That isn''t completely bad because a stock photo of a medal would probably naturally be centered. A big limiting factor is the subject holds a lot more interest for you than the casual viewer.  The title, I think, saves it, but not everybody reads the title.  It''s cute to thing how such a cheap trinket would mean so much to a child, but that is only conveyed with the title, not the picture.', '2006-05-31 14:47:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(2472353, 335854, 43410, '<td valign="top">congratulations on your first ribbon, and a blue at that!  great job :)<br/> <br/>enjoy your day, i know you''re excited</td>', 'congratulations on your first ribbon, and a blue at that!  great job :) enjoy your day, i know you''re excited', '2006-05-31 14:55:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(2472363, 338061, 31794, '<td valign="top">[[trading post]]<br/> <br/>this image is unfortunately not very good, when shooting on a white background you need multiple lights to keep the shadows away, and that color smear on the background is really bad.<br/> <br/>to get the background whiter in basic editing you can use selective color in photoshop and  select the white channel, then turn the black down until the background is bright white.<br/> <br/>but to get a higher score in this challenge I think the medallion has to be on the winner, to show a child as a winner always scores some points :)</td>', '[[trading post]] this image is unfortunately not very good, when shooting on a white background you need multiple lights to keep the shadows away, and that color smear on the background is really bad. to get the background whiter in basic editing you can use selective color in photoshop and  select the white channel, then turn the black down until the background is bright white. but to get a higher score in this challenge I think the medallion has to be on the winner, to show a child as a winner always scores some points :)', '2006-05-31 14:58:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(2472505, 338117, 11854, '<td valign="top">Trading post...<br/>  This is a cute shot. I like the setup and your little boy is adorable. The top (bottom) of the one foot is very distracting though. I''m not sure if that''s a blow out or maybe grass stains, LOL.</td>', 'Trading post...  This is a cute shot. I like the setup and your little boy is adorable. The top (bottom) of the one foot is very distracting though. I''m not sure if that''s a blow out or maybe grass stains, LOL.', '2006-05-31 15:43:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(2472514, 335854, 10134, '<td valign="top">ehhe... OF COURSE I''m excited today, jerowe !! I avow that i expected to get a good final mark with this picture, but with all my bad previous ''experiences'' on DPC, i didn''t believe i could win a day! I want to congratulate metatate, MacClavey and above all manic35 who''s been personally targeted by hell ugly trolls in this competition. To answer your question Yanko, the green background is almost the original color of my garden grass, i just set the highest saturation level available on my camera. And to all of you, thanks a LOT for all your encouraging (and also upcoming) comments!<br/> <br/>I dedicate this picture to my crusty Shui Ling and to another little bird that started a very difficult and short life... <br/> <br/>Antoine.<br/> <br/></td>', 'ehhe... OF COURSE I''m excited today, jerowe !! I avow that i expected to get a good final mark with this picture, but with all my bad previous ''experiences'' on DPC, i didn''t believe i could win a day! I want to congratulate metatate, MacClavey and above all manic35 who''s been personally targeted by hell ugly trolls in this competition. To answer your question Yanko, the green background is almost the original color of my garden grass, i just set the highest saturation level available on my camera. And to all of you, thanks a LOT for all your encouraging (and also upcoming) comments! I dedicate this picture to my crusty Shui Ling and to another little bird that started a very difficult and short life...  Antoine. ', '2006-05-31 15:47:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(2472517, 337675, 40718, '<td valign="top">You tried to fit a square peg into a round hole.  Simply does not convey the idea of success well enough.  Is she gabbing with her friend that she made the team?  Is she successful because she''s head cheerleader and most popular in school?  What gives?  Your one line makes me think this was a photo of opportunity and you relied on the title to try to get it to fit.  Apparently, it didn''t...<br/> <br/>You know the technicals as well as me.  It appears the Klieg lights were set more for theater than for photography.</td>', 'You tried to fit a square peg into a round hole.  Simply does not convey the idea of success well enough.  Is she gabbing with her friend that she made the team?  Is she successful because she''s head cheerleader and most popular in school?  What gives?  Your one line makes me think this was a photo of opportunity and you relied on the title to try to get it to fit.  Apparently, it didn''t... You know the technicals as well as me.  It appears the Klieg lights were set more for theater than for photography.', '2006-05-31 15:48:24.000000', NULL, 0),
