(2474293, 338141, 55642, '<td valign="top">Hi Laura -<br/> <br/>This is a unique take on the theme, but I''m not sure I would get the idea of "Success" from just looking at the photo. I actually think, "How sad, someone dropped their bagel!" Technically, there are several problems. First and foremost is that the top third of the photo is tremendously overblown. Besides that, the color seems off, perhaps too red. I think much of the light and color issues is due to the light source being behind  the subject, so my main suggestion for this shot is to light it more from the front, but diffusely to avoid glare since the bread (bagel?) is a bit shiny. Also, the bread/pastry is not well-centered, and is on the verge of being cut off on its rightmost edge. <br/> <br/>It does look like you got some good DoF along the cut edges of the bread, which works well for the ant.</td>', 'Hi Laura - This is a unique take on the theme, but I''m not sure I would get the idea of "Success" from just looking at the photo. I actually think, "How sad, someone dropped their bagel!" Technically, there are several problems. First and foremost is that the top third of the photo is tremendously overblown. Besides that, the color seems off, perhaps too red. I think much of the light and color issues is due to the light source being behind  the subject, so my main suggestion for this shot is to light it more from the front, but diffusely to avoid glare since the bread (bagel?) is a bit shiny. Also, the bread/pastry is not well-centered, and is on the verge of being cut off on its rightmost edge.  It does look like you got some good DoF along the cut edges of the bread, which works well for the ant.', '2006-05-31 23:12:55.000000', NULL, 0),
