(2483521, 335854, 10134, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by General:</b></div><hr/><i> Who gives 1,  to this  Photograph </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=341681<br/> <br/>"<br/>A troll''s story<br/>I give the best shots one''s, It''s such a rush !<br/>"<br/> <br/>so your answer is TROLLS. People who don''t even take a look at the pictures and who''ve found a good way to share their frustration...</td>', 'Originally posted by General: Who gives 1,  to this  Photograph   //www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=341681 "A troll''s storyI give the best shots one''s, It''s such a rush !" so your answer is TROLLS. People who don''t even take a look at the pictures and who''ve found a good way to share their frustration...', '2006-06-04 15:02:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(2483602, 338052, 41337, '<td valign="top">Congrats on the red. Btw, is that shutter speed correct? You must have one fast baby! :P</td>', 'Congrats on the red. Btw, is that shutter speed correct? You must have one fast baby! :P', '2006-06-04 15:38:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(2483606, 338143, 41337, '<td valign="top">The baby''s eyes looking up makes it all perfect.</td>', 'The baby''s eyes looking up makes it all perfect.', '2006-06-04 15:39:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(2483694, 338061, 14414, '<td valign="top"><br/><b><i>Composition </i></b> <br/>I would prefer the medal to be less centralized - maybe in the middle horizontally, but on the bottom third vertically<br/> <br/><b><i>Technical stuff (exposure, dof, lighting etc) </i></b> <br/>Focus is spot on, and exposure very good. I''m impressed with the lighting on the background to give a nice plain white b/g<br/> <br/><b><i>Post-processing </i></b> <br/>Not much to say really, good amount of saturation, good contrast<br/> <br/><b><i>Message/atmosphere portrayed </i></b> <br/>imho, if it were to include a grinning child, or the medal being held aloft for example, it would portray the desired feeling (of achievement, success, your kid''s pride...) a lot more.<br/> <br/><b><i>Meeting the challenge </i></b> <br/>Obviously<br/> <br/><b><i>My personal opinion </i></b> <br/>Whilst all the technicalities are good, the way you have approached the theme (imho) gives a rather clinical, stock photo kind of feel, rather than the emotions associated with the feeling of success.</td>', 'Composition  I would prefer the medal to be less centralized - maybe in the middle horizontally, but on the bottom third vertically Technical stuff (exposure, dof, lighting etc)  Focus is spot on, and exposure very good. I''m impressed with the lighting on the background to give a nice plain white b/g Post-processing  Not much to say really, good amount of saturation, good contrast Message/atmosphere portrayed  imho, if it were to include a grinning child, or the medal being held aloft for example, it would portray the desired feeling (of achievement, success, your kid''s pride...) a lot more. Meeting the challenge  Obviously My personal opinion  Whilst all the technicalities are good, the way you have approached the theme (imho) gives a rather clinical, stock photo kind of feel, rather than the emotions associated with the feeling of success.', '2006-06-04 16:08:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(2483733, 338129, 14414, '<td valign="top">First off, congrats on the personal best :)<br/> <br/><b><i>Composition </i></b> <br/>Lovely. The only thing I would change slightly is leaving a tiny bit more space on the  left, so that the spotlight is more centralized.<br/> <br/><b><i>Technical stuff (exposure, dof, lighting etc) </i></b> <br/>Lighting is beautiful, but seem to be blown highlighs on her face/arms/chest.  Focus is fine.<br/> <br/><b><i>Post-processing </i></b> <br/>only basic rules, so not much to say really. In advanced I would clone out that distreacting bit on the right.<br/> <br/><b><i>Message/atmosphere portrayed </i></b> <br/>Has a very elegant feel to it, and the crispness &amp; clean composition make it seem very professional, which really suits the subject matter.<br/> <br/><b><i>Meeting the challenge </i></b> <br/>I''m in 2 minds about this, tbh - it does fit the challenge, but to me says more about "performance" or "perfection" than  success.<br/> <br/><b><i>My personal opinion </i></b> <br/>Beautiful image, worthy of its place in the challenge. Well done!</td>', 'First off, congrats on the personal best :) Composition  Lovely. The only thing I would change slightly is leaving a tiny bit more space on the  left, so that the spotlight is more centralized. Technical stuff (exposure, dof, lighting etc)  Lighting is beautiful, but seem to be blown highlighs on her face/arms/chest.  Focus is fine. Post-processing  only basic rules, so not much to say really. In advanced I would clone out that distreacting bit on the right. Message/atmosphere portrayed  Has a very elegant feel to it, and the crispness & clean composition make it seem very professional, which really suits the subject matter. Meeting the challenge  I''m in 2 minds about this, tbh - it does fit the challenge, but to me says more about "performance" or "perfection" than  success. My personal opinion  Beautiful image, worthy of its place in the challenge. Well done!', '2006-06-04 16:23:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(2483809, 338158, 43434, '<td valign="top"><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>Wow .. always like these shots ... does this mean though that too many people do this?<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>This is a very centred shot.  Working towards the rule of thirds would help to create a different point of interest ... or taking a look at how to create a golden tringle ... something to take away that centre focus.<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>does it meet the challenge .. well it does if you are trying to successfully do a stop motion shot.  But others may not see it that way .. which is why I think there are a few DNMC type votes.<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>This is really an amazing colour ... it has a great depth as well.  so very unusual.  It is reasonably sharp and the lighting used here is perfect.<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>it is becoming a little cliched this type of shot .. but that should never put you off ... but work towards meet composition rules and see if that helps.<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>great shot ... good colours ... I am stunned. :)<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via<br/>the PM system.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari</td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club. First Impression - the most important one: Wow .. always like these shots ... does this mean though that too many people do this? Composition: This is a very centred shot.  Working towards the rule of thirds would help to create a different point of interest ... or taking a look at how to create a golden tringle ... something to take away that centre focus. Subject: does it meet the challenge .. well it does if you are trying to successfully do a stop motion shot.  But others may not see it that way .. which is why I think there are a few DNMC type votes. Technical (Colour and light): This is really an amazing colour ... it has a great depth as well.  so very unusual.  It is reasonably sharp and the lighting used here is perfect. To grow its vote?: it is becoming a little cliched this type of shot .. but that should never put you off ... but work towards meet composition rules and see if that helps. Summary: great shot ... good colours ... I am stunned. :) If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me viathe PM system. Cheers Kari', '2006-06-04 16:48:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(2483814, 335795, 43434, '<td valign="top"><br/><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>What a knotty situation ... you can tie and get it to hold to me that is success.<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>To me this shot is incredibly centred ... in that the knot itself runs down the centre line of the picture.  The balance to this is that the knot lines are also going up from left to right to create leading lines.  Maybe a different crop could have taken advantage of the leading line as well as placing the knot itself with the rule the thirds areas to create a little more interest. <br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>I think this meets the challenge well.<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>nice and sharp picture ... I perhaps would try a shallower DOF .. but not sure that would work.  I like the natural light of course.<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>try recropping and see what else you can capture through that.<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>Great shot  ... well done... I can see more good things comming.<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via<br/>the PM system.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari</td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club. First Impression - the most important one: What a knotty situation ... you can tie and get it to hold to me that is success. Composition: To me this shot is incredibly centred ... in that the knot itself runs down the centre line of the picture.  The balance to this is that the knot lines are also going up from left to right to create leading lines.  Maybe a different crop could have taken advantage of the leading line as well as placing the knot itself with the rule the thirds areas to create a little more interest.  Subject: I think this meets the challenge well. Technical (Colour and light): nice and sharp picture ... I perhaps would try a shallower DOF .. but not sure that would work.  I like the natural light of course. To grow its vote?: try recropping and see what else you can capture through that. Summary: Great shot  ... well done... I can see more good things comming. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me viathe PM system. Cheers Kari', '2006-06-04 16:54:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(2483838, 336201, 43434, '<td valign="top"><br/><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.  I know this is your first entry ... so hope this is not too painful.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>The picture is a little on the small side, maximising the entrys size is a great way to create impact from a shot ... you can work a picture up to 640 on the longest side.  You can also work it to 150 kbs .. which allows you much more data in a shot.<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>I like the lines going backwards and draging the eye into the shot .... I looked at your portfolio .. which is still empty I am not sure what you know about the simple rules of photography ... might pay to do a search on "rule of thirds" which is one i find really handy to take note of.<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>does it or doesn''t it ... I think you got a lot of people not knowing what you were trying to portray.  Once people can see you comments, you are ok .. but people can''t during voting .. so a picture must be able to carry itself. <br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>Black and white sometimes works .. but it doesn''t seem to add anything to this shot ... the colours may have worked better.  the slight flaring at the top of the picture is slightly distracting as well.<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>Think about how others will view the picture ... will they get it .. how much explaining do you need .. that sort of thing ... this is great to challenge peoples thinking outside the square . but sometimes that  doesn''t work either.<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>Good picture .. I can see good things coming from you in future ... keep it up.<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via<br/>the PM system.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari</td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.  I know this is your first entry ... so hope this is not too painful. First Impression - the most important one: The picture is a little on the small side, maximising the entrys size is a great way to create impact from a shot ... you can work a picture up to 640 on the longest side.  You can also work it to 150 kbs .. which allows you much more data in a shot. Composition: I like the lines going backwards and draging the eye into the shot .... I looked at your portfolio .. which is still empty I am not sure what you know about the simple rules of photography ... might pay to do a search on "rule of thirds" which is one i find really handy to take note of. Subject: does it or doesn''t it ... I think you got a lot of people not knowing what you were trying to portray.  Once people can see you comments, you are ok .. but people can''t during voting .. so a picture must be able to carry itself.  Technical (Colour and light): Black and white sometimes works .. but it doesn''t seem to add anything to this shot ... the colours may have worked better.  the slight flaring at the top of the picture is slightly distracting as well. To grow its vote?: Think about how others will view the picture ... will they get it .. how much explaining do you need .. that sort of thing ... this is great to challenge peoples thinking outside the square . but sometimes that  doesn''t work either. Summary: Good picture .. I can see good things coming from you in future ... keep it up. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me viathe PM system. Cheers Kari', '2006-06-04 17:09:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(2483861, 338129, 43434, '<td valign="top"><br/><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.<br/> <br/>Just a note ... every critique is a personal opinion .. it is up to you have you choose to use or ignore the information provided.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>Top ten .. wow ... lovely image .. well taken shot.<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>The works for this shot .. things I would think about are .. where am I taking the eye of the viewer ... how am I creating something that will hold a person for the moment longer .. I think that you have created something to hold a viewer for slightly longer but my eyes get slightly caught up on the blackness above her head and stays there.<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>Success like so many things in life is self-determined ... so yes I think this meets the challenge.<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>I like the reds and how this colours pops or the picture .. getting and taking the picture with her shadow is fantastic ... it feels a little close to the bottom of the shot .. was there more black that you could have used below this or the edge of the stage ...<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>Hey this got top ten .. which is fantastic ... to improve just try diffeernt crops etc.<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>Fantastic shot ... well done .. she is a beautiful woman is a beautful situation and you took great advantage of it all.<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via<br/>the PM system.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari</td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club. Just a note ... every critique is a personal opinion .. it is up to you have you choose to use or ignore the information provided. First Impression - the most important one: Top ten .. wow ... lovely image .. well taken shot. Composition: The works for this shot .. things I would think about are .. where am I taking the eye of the viewer ... how am I creating something that will hold a person for the moment longer .. I think that you have created something to hold a viewer for slightly longer but my eyes get slightly caught up on the blackness above her head and stays there. Subject: Success like so many things in life is self-determined ... so yes I think this meets the challenge. Technical (Colour and light): I like the reds and how this colours pops or the picture .. getting and taking the picture with her shadow is fantastic ... it feels a little close to the bottom of the shot .. was there more black that you could have used below this or the edge of the stage ... To grow its vote?: Hey this got top ten .. which is fantastic ... to improve just try diffeernt crops etc. Summary: Fantastic shot ... well done .. she is a beautiful woman is a beautful situation and you took great advantage of it all. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me viathe PM system. Cheers Kari', '2006-06-04 17:29:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(2483880, 337977, 43434, '<td valign="top"><br/><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.<br/> <br/>Interesting to read the comments you have recieved ... they are helpful from what I see .. if you feel they are helpful please tick the box so that the person making them knows that.<br/> <br/>There are some interesting personal opinions in these comments .. and it is up to you what you take on board .. ... alll critiques are of course personal opinion ... choose to use the information as you like.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>Interesting shot ... I want a bit more ... something more of the story in the picture.<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>The picture is very centred around the childs face.  have a try at google and enter '' rule of thirds'' this is a really  good starting rule to learn ... I found that it has helped take me from very basic and centred shots to thinking about the composition more and what else the viewer needs to see to balance a shot.<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>Every child is a success story to their parent ... success is also a self determed thing .. ones success may be anothers failure ... your success is great though.<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>The focus is not good ... it is not too bad in the thumbnail .. but people vote on the larger image.  the catchlights in her eyes are lovely though ... this is a good thing .... <br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>Working on getting things focused helps ... this in itself is a skill ... trust me I am still good at unfocused shots .. but I have learnt not to enter them as this is something that gets scored badly.  This is a pretty picture .. but people do look for a story in picture .. maybe in her mothers arms that would have told a story a little better.<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>You did ok ... you are going to do better and improve ... keep shooting and this will come naturally.<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via<br/>the PM system.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari</td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club. Interesting to read the comments you have recieved ... they are helpful from what I see .. if you feel they are helpful please tick the box so that the person making them knows that. There are some interesting personal opinions in these comments .. and it is up to you what you take on board .. ... alll critiques are of course personal opinion ... choose to use the information as you like. First Impression - the most important one: Interesting shot ... I want a bit more ... something more of the story in the picture. Composition: The picture is very centred around the childs face.  have a try at google and enter '' rule of thirds'' this is a really  good starting rule to learn ... I found that it has helped take me from very basic and centred shots to thinking about the composition more and what else the viewer needs to see to balance a shot. Subject: Every child is a success story to their parent ... success is also a self determed thing .. ones success may be anothers failure ... your success is great though. Technical (Colour and light): The focus is not good ... it is not too bad in the thumbnail .. but people vote on the larger image.  the catchlights in her eyes are lovely though ... this is a good thing ....  To grow its vote?: Working on getting things focused helps ... this in itself is a skill ... trust me I am still good at unfocused shots .. but I have learnt not to enter them as this is something that gets scored badly.  This is a pretty picture .. but people do look for a story in picture .. maybe in her mothers arms that would have told a story a little better. Summary: You did ok ... you are going to do better and improve ... keep shooting and this will come naturally. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me viathe PM system. Cheers Kari', '2006-06-04 17:41:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(2483897, 338321, 43434, '<td valign="top"><br/><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>What stop motion.  You should be proud and i can see the happy dance going on .... you did great ... <br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>This picture draws the viewer in and takes me further in ... I think it is really cool that you don''t included the whole bird .. as my imagination needs working and in working completes the image.<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>Great choice.<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>Natural is always good.  <br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>I don''t know what you can do ... this is just too good anyways.<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>Congrats and well done .. keep it up.<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via<br/>the PM system.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari</td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club. First Impression - the most important one: What stop motion.  You should be proud and i can see the happy dance going on .... you did great ...  Composition: This picture draws the viewer in and takes me further in ... I think it is really cool that you don''t included the whole bird .. as my imagination needs working and in working completes the image. Subject: Great choice. Technical (Colour and light): Natural is always good.   To grow its vote?: I don''t know what you can do ... this is just too good anyways. Summary: Congrats and well done .. keep it up. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me viathe PM system. Cheers Kari', '2006-06-04 17:52:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(2483932, 336791, 43434, '<td valign="top"><br/><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>First entry ... you done good.  <br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>This is a little centered to me ... cropping off some of the blank space of the left .. and getting the flower on the the thirds would have helped this shot .. and enhanced what the eye is looking for - a point of focus.<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>Success is self determined . .what works for some doesn''t for others ... this is a fine interpretation.<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>This is where things get murky.   You really needed something in focus .. and since the flower is the thing we are looking at .. it needed to be more in focus.  The flying buds did not ... the stem seems to be the focus point .. so it is about getting the camera to focus slightly up from where it did.  the bright areas at the back of the picture .. don''t really add anything to this shot .. so trying different crops may also help.<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>Try and try again .. that is what it is about .. I always ask .. will someone else get this .. does it say enough in the picture itself.<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>good work .. a lovely first entry .. keep shooting entering and learning.<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via<br/>the PM system.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari</td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club. First Impression - the most important one: First entry ... you done good.   Composition: This is a little centered to me ... cropping off some of the blank space of the left .. and getting the flower on the the thirds would have helped this shot .. and enhanced what the eye is looking for - a point of focus. Subject: Success is self determined . .what works for some doesn''t for others ... this is a fine interpretation. Technical (Colour and light): This is where things get murky.   You really needed something in focus .. and since the flower is the thing we are looking at .. it needed to be more in focus.  The flying buds did not ... the stem seems to be the focus point .. so it is about getting the camera to focus slightly up from where it did.  the bright areas at the back of the picture .. don''t really add anything to this shot .. so trying different crops may also help. To grow its vote?: Try and try again .. that is what it is about .. I always ask .. will someone else get this .. does it say enough in the picture itself. Summary: good work .. a lovely first entry .. keep shooting entering and learning. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me viathe PM system. Cheers Kari', '2006-06-04 18:12:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(2483948, 337607, 43434, '<td valign="top"><br/><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>Great capture .. this epitomises success to me.<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>This is ok ... you have him place squarely on thirds .. and its just a natural type of shot.<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>as mentioned above meets the challenge ... and does with total determination.<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>Natural works best ... often .. and here works great.  The focus is a little soft .. but it is hard taking candids and harder when they are moving ... maybe a fast shutter speed would have helped - but not sure ... <br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>I would have tried a tighter crop .. the person on the left and the car are both destractions.<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>this worked ok .. you are learning and applying what you learn ... good work.<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via<br/>the PM system.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari</td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club. First Impression - the most important one: Great capture .. this epitomises success to me. Composition: This is ok ... you have him place squarely on thirds .. and its just a natural type of shot. Subject: as mentioned above meets the challenge ... and does with total determination. Technical (Colour and light): Natural works best ... often .. and here works great.  The focus is a little soft .. but it is hard taking candids and harder when they are moving ... maybe a fast shutter speed would have helped - but not sure ...  To grow its vote?: I would have tried a tighter crop .. the person on the left and the car are both destractions. Summary: this worked ok .. you are learning and applying what you learn ... good work. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me viathe PM system. Cheers Kari', '2006-06-04 18:19:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(2483969, 337530, 43434, '<td valign="top"><br/><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>You are so right ....I think this is a great out of the box shot.<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>The composition is fine .. the dirt track is almost on thirds and the top of the cages are working towards that are well.<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>So what ... success is self determined .. .and starting is always a good  place to begin.<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>your aperture you included in your comments it is the f stop information so is 3.8.<br/> <br/>Colours are great and sharp for something with so much movement. <br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>Think about how others will see the image ... I think this is one from left field .. and for me that works .. for others they like to be spoon fed the normal type o stuff... you have a good eye use it.<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>Great work for a first entry fantastic.<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari</td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club. First Impression - the most important one: You are so right ....I think this is a great out of the box shot. Composition: The composition is fine .. the dirt track is almost on thirds and the top of the cages are working towards that are well. Subject: So what ... success is self determined .. .and starting is always a good  place to begin. Technical (Colour and light): your aperture you included in your comments it is the f stop information so is 3.8. Colours are great and sharp for something with so much movement.  To grow its vote?: Think about how others will see the image ... I think this is one from left field .. and for me that works .. for others they like to be spoon fed the normal type o stuff... you have a good eye use it. Summary: Great work for a first entry fantastic. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system. Cheers Kari', '2006-06-04 18:28:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(2483990, 337818, 43434, '<td valign="top"><br/><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>Out of the box .. and slamming from left feild.  I like it .. but others may have issues with the nature of the picture.<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>I find the composition a little boring ... sorry ... think about backgrounds .. think about the rules of photograpy including rule of thirds (you should google this) .... I would also consider a reshoot taking into account the rules.  <br/> <br/>Consider the following<br/> <br/>Girl perched on stool with one leg up hair and face as above.... and whip dangling over knee ... cropping the shot to exlude the full length of the stool ... so it is a tigher crop on the model .. but still captures the boot and the whip in a slightly different way ... just a thought.<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>Will you got hit by the DNMC vote .. big time.  I find this really funny . I did not vote on this challenge ... but I think that for some this image really will epitomise success .. being that success is self determined.<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>The picture is a little flat/lifeless .. trying a little more on the contrast and the curves may help to eliminate this feeling.<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>Well meeting the challenge how others see it would help ... apart from that think about backgrounds and bringing life into a picture.<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>Interesting work .. keep it up.  Be interesting to see what you come up with next.<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via<br/>the PM system.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari</td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club. First Impression - the most important one: Out of the box .. and slamming from left feild.  I like it .. but others may have issues with the nature of the picture. Composition: I find the composition a little boring ... sorry ... think about backgrounds .. think about the rules of photograpy including rule of thirds (you should google this) .... I would also consider a reshoot taking into account the rules.   Consider the following Girl perched on stool with one leg up hair and face as above.... and whip dangling over knee ... cropping the shot to exlude the full length of the stool ... so it is a tigher crop on the model .. but still captures the boot and the whip in a slightly different way ... just a thought. Subject: Will you got hit by the DNMC vote .. big time.  I find this really funny . I did not vote on this challenge ... but I think that for some this image really will epitomise success .. being that success is self determined. Technical (Colour and light): The picture is a little flat/lifeless .. trying a little more on the contrast and the curves may help to eliminate this feeling. To grow its vote?: Well meeting the challenge how others see it would help ... apart from that think about backgrounds and bringing life into a picture. Summary: Interesting work .. keep it up.  Be interesting to see what you come up with next. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me viathe PM system. Cheers Kari', '2006-06-04 18:39:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(2483993, 337366, 43434, '<td valign="top">Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>ones success is anothers failure.  This picture could have worked in either .. but as a failure I think may have excelled.<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>I think there is too much in this capture.  If you had cropped tighter on the action this may have added to the picture.  But it also may have shown the soft focus of the shot .. being that the goalie is moving a lot.<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>mets the challenge .. but as mentioned may have excelled in the other one.<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>This is  great ... good natural light .. and lovely sharp colours and lines.<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>You did good for the shot you entered .. enter a different crop it would be a different story .. I am not sure it would be better though.<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>Good work .. .something totally new for you from a quick look at your portfolio ...<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via<br/>the PM system.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari</td>', 'Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club. First Impression - the most important one: ones success is anothers failure.  This picture could have worked in either .. but as a failure I think may have excelled. Composition: I think there is too much in this capture.  If you had cropped tighter on the action this may have added to the picture.  But it also may have shown the soft focus of the shot .. being that the goalie is moving a lot. Subject: mets the challenge .. but as mentioned may have excelled in the other one. Technical (Colour and light): This is  great ... good natural light .. and lovely sharp colours and lines. To grow its vote?: You did good for the shot you entered .. enter a different crop it would be a different story .. I am not sure it would be better though. Summary: Good work .. .something totally new for you from a quick look at your portfolio ... If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me viathe PM system. Cheers Kari', '2006-06-04 18:45:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(2484021, 337084, 43434, '<td valign="top"><br/><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>This is a lovely image, seems a little too tightly cropped.<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>The crop doesn''t allow the rules to apply easerly .. I am not sure but it just doesn''t seem to work well .. maybe working towards the rule of thirds would have helped in the circumstance .. do a google on this and see how that helps in recropping and positioning of the people in the frame.<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>I think lots of people did not get/understand the success shown .. so got a littl of the DNMC ... but I think it meets the challenge fine.<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>Not sharp enough .. you mentioned this .. I think that the border is a little too thick and creates a tightness on the image.  I like the colours they are lovely and bright.<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>Think about the rules of photography .. i am not at home so don''t have my normal URLs to give .. but this may help in future ... do a google and have a look around.<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>Good work .. keep it up.<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via<br/>the PM system.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari</td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club. First Impression - the most important one: This is a lovely image, seems a little too tightly cropped. Composition: The crop doesn''t allow the rules to apply easerly .. I am not sure but it just doesn''t seem to work well .. maybe working towards the rule of thirds would have helped in the circumstance .. do a google on this and see how that helps in recropping and positioning of the people in the frame. Subject: I think lots of people did not get/understand the success shown .. so got a littl of the DNMC ... but I think it meets the challenge fine. Technical (Colour and light): Not sharp enough .. you mentioned this .. I think that the border is a little too thick and creates a tightness on the image.  I like the colours they are lovely and bright. To grow its vote?: Think about the rules of photography .. i am not at home so don''t have my normal URLs to give .. but this may help in future ... do a google and have a look around. Summary: Good work .. keep it up. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me viathe PM system. Cheers Kari', '2006-06-04 19:04:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(2484037, 337902, 43434, '<td valign="top"><br/><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>Very ole worldy.  kinda a cool concept.<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>A little more cropping on the right would have moved the little girl into the thirds line nicely and not detracted from the shot.   The hill creates a lovely leading line for the eye to follow.<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>Well the title meets the challenge ... but i am not sure the picture could stand on its own.<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>lovely sepia tonings and natural light.  The picture is a little soft focus on the kids though.<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>There are a couple of things ... crop tightly on the kids to include less of the shed but have it peeking at the right of the shot ... this would have created a focus on the kids and their holding of the bible.<br/> <br/>Also think about how the shot stands without the title itself.<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>Good shot .. and lovely image well done.<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via<br/>the PM system.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari</td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club. First Impression - the most important one: Very ole worldy.  kinda a cool concept. Composition: A little more cropping on the right would have moved the little girl into the thirds line nicely and not detracted from the shot.   The hill creates a lovely leading line for the eye to follow. Subject: Well the title meets the challenge ... but i am not sure the picture could stand on its own. Technical (Colour and light): lovely sepia tonings and natural light.  The picture is a little soft focus on the kids though. To grow its vote?: There are a couple of things ... crop tightly on the kids to include less of the shed but have it peeking at the right of the shot ... this would have created a focus on the kids and their holding of the bible. Also think about how the shot stands without the title itself. Summary: Good shot .. and lovely image well done. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me viathe PM system. Cheers Kari', '2006-06-04 19:10:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(2484052, 338203, 43434, '<td valign="top"><br/><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>I prefer sumo snails to league anyday and I am a kiwi!  <br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>I love this shot and the crop, a minor adjustment to the top of the shot would have put the snails heads right on thirds ... not sure it would have helped but technical people would have picked that up.<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>I don''t think the DNMC got you I think the lack of understanding the sumo rules did ... cos this picture epitomises success in sumo.<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>love the colours and lighting.  I have never really taken such a close look at snails so this is really cool .. and no I am also not on drugs.<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>Tell people the rules of the game then they will get it ... bloody hard that one.<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>I think this is so out of left field it is fantastic .. I am sorry that it did not do better ... but that is peoples opinions for ya.<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via<br/>the PM system.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari</td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club. First Impression - the most important one: I prefer sumo snails to league anyday and I am a kiwi!   Composition: I love this shot and the crop, a minor adjustment to the top of the shot would have put the snails heads right on thirds ... not sure it would have helped but technical people would have picked that up. Subject: I don''t think the DNMC got you I think the lack of understanding the sumo rules did ... cos this picture epitomises success in sumo. Technical (Colour and light): love the colours and lighting.  I have never really taken such a close look at snails so this is really cool .. and no I am also not on drugs. To grow its vote?: Tell people the rules of the game then they will get it ... bloody hard that one. Summary: I think this is so out of left field it is fantastic .. I am sorry that it did not do better ... but that is peoples opinions for ya. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me viathe PM system. Cheers Kari', '2006-06-04 19:16:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(2484104, 338082, 43434, '<td valign="top"><br/><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>Great colours ... good DOF .. almost could be used as one of those inspirational posters they have in the workplace.<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>the head of the seed is almost perfectly on thirds .. which technically is kinda cool.  <br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>Without the title ... does this meet the challenge .. not sure .. but I think that this does on other levels really well.<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>I love the colours you have captured so well.<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>only take shots that meet the knowledge and understanding of success of the majority ... none of these left field/out of the box looks.   <br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>I think you did great.... keep it up.<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via<br/>the PM system.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari</td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club. First Impression - the most important one: Great colours ... good DOF .. almost could be used as one of those inspirational posters they have in the workplace. Composition: the head of the seed is almost perfectly on thirds .. which technically is kinda cool.   Subject: Without the title ... does this meet the challenge .. not sure .. but I think that this does on other levels really well. Technical (Colour and light): I love the colours you have captured so well. To grow its vote?: only take shots that meet the knowledge and understanding of success of the majority ... none of these left field/out of the box looks.    Summary: I think you did great.... keep it up. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me viathe PM system. Cheers Kari', '2006-06-04 19:38:11.000000', NULL, 0),
