(2484146, 337982, 43434, '<td valign="top"><br/><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>busy and colourful and full on.<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>This is so busy bit the main focus of the main medal with the two side verticals is extremely centred, which is a little off putting.<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>This is interesting for some this would meet the challenge, and others like me would go ... so what - this actually doesn''t mean anything to a lot of people and I don''t think that helped in the voting.  I have been caught out by this a number of times with people not understanding the significance of a shot.<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>This works well .. I like the lighting and the fantastic range of colours.<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>Appeal to the populace ... so hard to do ... <br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>Great eye and good shooting .. keep it up.<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via<br/>the PM system.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari</td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club. First Impression - the most important one: busy and colourful and full on. Composition: This is so busy bit the main focus of the main medal with the two side verticals is extremely centred, which is a little off putting. Subject: This is interesting for some this would meet the challenge, and others like me would go ... so what - this actually doesn''t mean anything to a lot of people and I don''t think that helped in the voting.  I have been caught out by this a number of times with people not understanding the significance of a shot. Technical (Colour and light): This works well .. I like the lighting and the fantastic range of colours. To grow its vote?: Appeal to the populace ... so hard to do ...  Summary: Great eye and good shooting .. keep it up. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me viathe PM system. Cheers Kari', '2006-06-04 19:56:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(2484180, 337271, 43434, '<td valign="top"><br/><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>Interesting concept for success, and it is a real success for some of us.<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>This is where I think some of the issues come from for the voters.  Do a google search on rule of thirds and golden triange ... looking at how to apply these to a shot really helps in getting an image on its way to better scoring. <br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>meets the challenge, I don''t understand the level of low soring onthis image.  It blows me away that you have so many low scores and one comment.<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>I think that this is good .. the picture is sharp for an action shot.  I think I would have preferred a different angle, maybe a slight bit behind to get the boy actually hit the ball.<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>take a look at the higher scorers and see what they have done, this is one of the best ways to learn ... it won''t take long to start picking up some of the methods used by others.<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>Good solid portfolio pic.  keep it up.<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via<br/>the PM system.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari</td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club. First Impression - the most important one: Interesting concept for success, and it is a real success for some of us. Composition: This is where I think some of the issues come from for the voters.  Do a google search on rule of thirds and golden triange ... looking at how to apply these to a shot really helps in getting an image on its way to better scoring.  Subject: meets the challenge, I don''t understand the level of low soring onthis image.  It blows me away that you have so many low scores and one comment. Technical (Colour and light): I think that this is good .. the picture is sharp for an action shot.  I think I would have preferred a different angle, maybe a slight bit behind to get the boy actually hit the ball. To grow its vote?: take a look at the higher scorers and see what they have done, this is one of the best ways to learn ... it won''t take long to start picking up some of the methods used by others. Summary: Good solid portfolio pic.  keep it up. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me viathe PM system. Cheers Kari', '2006-06-04 20:13:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(2484239, 337116, 43434, '<td valign="top"><br/><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>Good shot ... interesting to a degree ... again it is the title that makes the image success and that is where in scoring I think the issues happen.<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>Well done, good crop  ... and god thirds.<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>Meets the challenge with the title .. doesn''t without it ... that is the issue I think with the scoring.<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>Good lighting, sharp image, and great colours.<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>have the image itself meet the challenge with little add from the title itself.<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>well done , i think a shot to be proud of.<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via<br/>the PM system.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari</td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club. First Impression - the most important one: Good shot ... interesting to a degree ... again it is the title that makes the image success and that is where in scoring I think the issues happen. Composition: Well done, good crop  ... and god thirds. Subject: Meets the challenge with the title .. doesn''t without it ... that is the issue I think with the scoring. Technical (Colour and light): Good lighting, sharp image, and great colours. To grow its vote?: have the image itself meet the challenge with little add from the title itself. Summary: well done , i think a shot to be proud of. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me viathe PM system. Cheers Kari', '2006-06-04 20:40:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(2484254, 336678, 43434, '<td valign="top"><br/><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>Seems more of a snapshot than an image that was thought out and composed, I think this is a candid, which is great, but in order to really make something of the shot you needed to capture what was realy happening, perhaps a closer shot of the kid lighting the candle .. not so much background and distracting elements.<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>I think the this is ok .. but personally a close up of the kid may have been better as the other elements add little to the shot.<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>With the title it meets the challenge but without it it doesn''t say much.  It is hard to convey to others the importance of what is taking place without the story for this image.<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>Nice colours good lighting.<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>Think about the crop .. maybe getting down on the ground to capture the actual event ... perhaps even having it so we can read one of the bottles.<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>Good pic, well done.<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via<br/>the PM system.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari</td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club. First Impression - the most important one: Seems more of a snapshot than an image that was thought out and composed, I think this is a candid, which is great, but in order to really make something of the shot you needed to capture what was realy happening, perhaps a closer shot of the kid lighting the candle .. not so much background and distracting elements. Composition: I think the this is ok .. but personally a close up of the kid may have been better as the other elements add little to the shot. Subject: With the title it meets the challenge but without it it doesn''t say much.  It is hard to convey to others the importance of what is taking place without the story for this image. Technical (Colour and light): Nice colours good lighting. To grow its vote?: Think about the crop .. maybe getting down on the ground to capture the actual event ... perhaps even having it so we can read one of the bottles. Summary: Good pic, well done. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me viathe PM system. Cheers Kari', '2006-06-04 20:47:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(2484261, 338286, 43434, '<td valign="top"><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>Nothing is new.<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>This shot lacks the use of the basic rules of composition, take a look on google at the rule of thirds and see how this can help improve the composition of this shot.<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>does it or not ... really self determined in this shot.  This doesn''t show the entry being made and enterd .. it only shows the clock on the computer.<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>The colours is very yellow cast, this will be due to the lighting in the room.<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>Think about how others are going to see the image, this is an inside joke and similar have been done a number of times I don''t think any as done well.<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>From your portfolio you have some good work, can''t wait to see of it in the challenges.<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via<br/>the PM system.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari</td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club. First Impression - the most important one: Nothing is new. Composition: This shot lacks the use of the basic rules of composition, take a look on google at the rule of thirds and see how this can help improve the composition of this shot. Subject: does it or not ... really self determined in this shot.  This doesn''t show the entry being made and enterd .. it only shows the clock on the computer. Technical (Colour and light): The colours is very yellow cast, this will be due to the lighting in the room. To grow its vote?: Think about how others are going to see the image, this is an inside joke and similar have been done a number of times I don''t think any as done well. Summary: From your portfolio you have some good work, can''t wait to see of it in the challenges. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me viathe PM system. Cheers Kari', '2006-06-04 20:51:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(2484280, 337195, 43434, '<td valign="top"><br/><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>You got the cute vote .. I can tell by the comments.  This is sooooooo cute it ain''t funny.<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>is a lovely shot but very centred ... which is a minor for this shot.<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>meets the challenge and does so in a cute and fuzzy way.<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>i really like this ...it is reasonbly dark which has been picked up by some commentors, but I don''t see this detracting from the natural shot. <br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>Take it from another angle .. front on capture the look from the eyes ... hehehe (I think you did well with a nature shot)<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>Great work ... fantastic capture.<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via<br/>the PM system.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari</td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club. First Impression - the most important one: You got the cute vote .. I can tell by the comments.  This is sooooooo cute it ain''t funny. Composition: is a lovely shot but very centred ... which is a minor for this shot. Subject: meets the challenge and does so in a cute and fuzzy way. Technical (Colour and light): i really like this ...it is reasonbly dark which has been picked up by some commentors, but I don''t see this detracting from the natural shot.  To grow its vote?: Take it from another angle .. front on capture the look from the eyes ... hehehe (I think you did well with a nature shot) Summary: Great work ... fantastic capture. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me viathe PM system. Cheers Kari', '2006-06-04 21:04:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(2484298, 337004, 43434, '<td valign="top"><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>I think that this is a love it or hate it shot.  <br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>This is the area I think that it lacks most.  It is not working to any rule of photography that I know (and I don''t know many) .. .and just seems like a little something in the courner of a whole big picture of a doorstep.<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>It does say success ... even though I don''t think it is a four leaf clover it is still a brave plant to grow in that little gap.<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>The colours are over saturated with the red being too red.  I think there is a little too much bakground in this shot and with a tighter crop on the growth it may have done better. <br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>You did ok ... keeep it up.<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>A good safe shot .. you have a great eye for the unusual.  <br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via<br/>the PM system.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari<br/> <br/>So cool to have a response  and it is amazing that the colours are natural .. I don''t think I have ever seen any that are so crisp as these.  <br/> <br/>I appreciate your response ... and am always happy to hear from someone I have reviewed.<br/> <br/>Cheers again<br/> <br/>Kari<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-06-04 23:25:53.</i></td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club. First Impression - the most important one: I think that this is a love it or hate it shot.   Composition: This is the area I think that it lacks most.  It is not working to any rule of photography that I know (and I don''t know many) .. .and just seems like a little something in the courner of a whole big picture of a doorstep. Subject: It does say success ... even though I don''t think it is a four leaf clover it is still a brave plant to grow in that little gap. Technical (Colour and light): The colours are over saturated with the red being too red.  I think there is a little too much bakground in this shot and with a tighter crop on the growth it may have done better.  To grow its vote?: You did ok ... keeep it up. Summary: A good safe shot .. you have a great eye for the unusual.   If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me viathe PM system. Cheers Kari So cool to have a response  and it is amazing that the colours are natural .. I don''t think I have ever seen any that are so crisp as these.   I appreciate your response ... and am always happy to hear from someone I have reviewed. Cheers again Kari', '2006-06-04 21:12:30.000000', '2006-06-05 00:25:53.000000', 0),
(2484445, 338279, 36371, '<td valign="top">Wonderful feeling to this pic. Just love the lighting and detail. Thanks for sharing this.<br/>From one Becky to another....<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-06-04 21:19:55.</i></td>', 'Wonderful feeling to this pic. Just love the lighting and detail. Thanks for sharing this.From one Becky to another....', '2006-06-04 22:19:17.000000', '2006-06-04 22:19:55.000000', 0),
(2484476, 337004, 9509, '<td valign="top">Kari,<br/> <br/>I appreciate your critique of my image.<br/> <br/>The subject is not a four-leaf clover, it is some tropical plant that had taken root in the back alley of a bar in Key West.<br/> <br/>The image saturation was not edited...the brick sidewalk was definetly that red...and the plant was so close to the wall and the sun so bright that it''s color reflected on the wall.<br/> <br/>As for there being too much background...I felt that it was needed to let you realize it''s small stature against the massive building.<br/> <br/>I certainly appreciate your review, my explainations of the image is not because what you said upset me...I will keep them in mind.<br/> <br/>thanks,<br/> <br/>Hank</td>', 'Kari, I appreciate your critique of my image. The subject is not a four-leaf clover, it is some tropical plant that had taken root in the back alley of a bar in Key West. The image saturation was not edited...the brick sidewalk was definetly that red...and the plant was so close to the wall and the sun so bright that it''s color reflected on the wall. As for there being too much background...I felt that it was needed to let you realize it''s small stature against the massive building. I certainly appreciate your review, my explainations of the image is not because what you said upset me...I will keep them in mind. thanks, Hank', '2006-06-04 22:38:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(2484806, 337194, 43434, '<td valign="top"><br/><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>Wow .. an achievement indeed.<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>Thsi is lovely for this shot .. the child looking outside ensures that our eyes are captivated by whatever has him under a spell.<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>Lovely meets the challenge, really weird the amount of subjects that do as success is really self determined.<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>The focus is a little soft ... but colours and lighting are fine.<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>Well it is hard to know really ... as this is so subjetive, I think that a lot of people do not understand a child is a success so it is really rolling with the punches.<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>Lovely shot .. always hold him in pride of heart.<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via<br/>the PM system.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari</td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club. First Impression - the most important one: Wow .. an achievement indeed. Composition: Thsi is lovely for this shot .. the child looking outside ensures that our eyes are captivated by whatever has him under a spell. Subject: Lovely meets the challenge, really weird the amount of subjects that do as success is really self determined. Technical (Colour and light): The focus is a little soft ... but colours and lighting are fine. To grow its vote?: Well it is hard to know really ... as this is so subjetive, I think that a lot of people do not understand a child is a success so it is really rolling with the punches. Summary: Lovely shot .. always hold him in pride of heart. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me viathe PM system. Cheers Kari', '2006-06-05 00:40:18.000000', NULL, 0),
