(2542053, 338332, 53585, '<td valign="top">Nice idea,I see your dressed alike also.</td>', 'Nice idea,I see your dressed alike also.', '2006-06-22 18:18:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(2546159, 336198, 46314, '<td valign="top">Not a bad pic. The composition is decent - strong subject. A level shoreline might have made a stronger impact though (parallel bands of colour behind a subject usually emphasise the subject well). And there is good focus (although you could probably sharpen it up a bit more in pp).<br/> <br/>Two things probably hurt your votes - firstly the lack of a more solid connection between your image and the theme. Most people tend to overlook the title...<br/> <br/>And secondly, the overall tone is a bit flat. Needed to pump up the contrast and the colours a bit. On this site, photographers usually talk of getting their images to ''pop''. That''s a good description of what I mean - if it was more vivid it would burst out at your eyes more.<br/> <br/>Cute chick though... ;-)</td>', 'Not a bad pic. The composition is decent - strong subject. A level shoreline might have made a stronger impact though (parallel bands of colour behind a subject usually emphasise the subject well). And there is good focus (although you could probably sharpen it up a bit more in pp). Two things probably hurt your votes - firstly the lack of a more solid connection between your image and the theme. Most people tend to overlook the title... And secondly, the overall tone is a bit flat. Needed to pump up the contrast and the colours a bit. On this site, photographers usually talk of getting their images to ''pop''. That''s a good description of what I mean - if it was more vivid it would burst out at your eyes more. Cute chick though... ;-)', '2006-06-23 19:06:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(2550355, 337014, 36470, '<td valign="top">This is an adorable candid shot.  Love the white on white.  Much deserved top 10!</td>', 'This is an adorable candid shot.  Love the white on white.  Much deserved top 10!', '2006-06-25 01:33:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(2572580, 338117, 43031, '<td valign="top">I think that the idea here was good, but the execution was lacking. I think it does show success in a certain way. I also think that many really don''t understand success in a healthy manner, which leads them not to understand how this fits the challenge. <br/> <br/>The execution part: Portraits of any kind, even far away and under trees, are better with directional lighting than with full daylight. The light is so incredibly even on you, that it almost seems you could be pasted in. I''m thinking you may have meant for the shaft of light to highlight your son, but the light then became too harsh. Also, this shot setup I think works better with much negative space instead of busy space that you see here. Maybe you two sitting on a hillside with mostly blue sky above you. Maybe that or this in provia black and white.<br/> <br/>I also get in those moods where I just want to take a picture for me and ignore all the artsy crud, but I and you should probably resist entering these photo''s, and just enjoy them on our walls. (I also do stupid too-literal stuff like my bokeh entry)</td>', 'I think that the idea here was good, but the execution was lacking. I think it does show success in a certain way. I also think that many really don''t understand success in a healthy manner, which leads them not to understand how this fits the challenge.  The execution part: Portraits of any kind, even far away and under trees, are better with directional lighting than with full daylight. The light is so incredibly even on you, that it almost seems you could be pasted in. I''m thinking you may have meant for the shaft of light to highlight your son, but the light then became too harsh. Also, this shot setup I think works better with much negative space instead of busy space that you see here. Maybe you two sitting on a hillside with mostly blue sky above you. Maybe that or this in provia black and white. I also get in those moods where I just want to take a picture for me and ignore all the artsy crud, but I and you should probably resist entering these photo''s, and just enjoy them on our walls. (I also do stupid too-literal stuff like my bokeh entry)', '2006-07-01 16:57:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(2594491, 337607, 51538, '<td valign="top">This has the potential for a great photo.  But to realize the potential, one would have to set up the shot and have a model pose.  It''s interesting how snaps of life as it passes by one can lead further into the creative process.  The lad is pretty happy and looks good too.  Might be hard - but not impossible - to emulate in a posed shot.</td>', 'This has the potential for a great photo.  But to realize the potential, one would have to set up the shot and have a model pose.  It''s interesting how snaps of life as it passes by one can lead further into the creative process.  The lad is pretty happy and looks good too.  Might be hard - but not impossible - to emulate in a posed shot.', '2006-07-06 19:26:58.000000', NULL, 0),
